38-\begin{itemize}
39-\item We present the first method that internalizes SDF collision geometry into VLA flow-matching weights during training, producing a model that generates inherently collision-aware actions with zero inference overhead. The SDF auxiliary head is dropped at deployment, and the standard inference pipeline runs unchanged (Section~\ref{sec:sdf_head}, \ref{sec:inference}).
40-\item We propose a noise-aware collision-shaping loss with a time-dependent weight function $w(t)$ that adapts to the flow-matching noise schedule, activating collision penalties only in the low-noise regime where the model's geometric predictions carry reliable spatial information. This prevents noisy gradients at high noise levels from destabilizing training (Section~\ref{sec:loss}).
